  {
    "id": "PSF-015685",
    "ref": "pge:14493-lz",
    "name": "Punod Landing",
    "lat": 10.5093,
    "lon": 123.333,
    "wind": {},
    "altitude": 305.0,
    "sources": {
      "pge": "14493-lz"
    },
    "primary": "pge",
    "role": "landing",
    "tow": false,
    "group": [
      "pge:14493"
    ],
    "notes": "There is a top landing option north of the take off location, and one passes on the way to launch site from the road.(see photos).\r\n\r\nBottom landing options are basically cultivated areas in the valley below. The easiest landing area I've found is marked on the map and there is a photo shown below.(Not easy to see from take off). However, this is quite a bit below the road and a bit of a climb out, but the farmer there is happy to help & carry the bag. There is a slop landing option just above the road almost due East of launch, but you need to be careful to stay clear of the trees.",
    "url": "https://www.paraglidingearth.com/?site=14493"
  },
